{# How to find the passages and the pages that answer a question, in many documents or in
   one. Each sentence that names a tool renders only when the run has it. #}
Finding passages and pages

{% if has('search_passages') %}
To search many documents, use {{ tool('search_passages') }}. It searches the text passages by keywords and by meaning together. Use it for a question in plain words, when the words that the documents use are not clear. Give up to 12 queries in one call, each a different form of the question. Each hit names the queries that found it. For an exact name, an address or a phrase, use {{ tool('search_collections') }}.

{% endif %}
{% if has('doc_search_text') or has('pdf_search') %}
To search one long document, use these tools.
{% if has('doc_search_text') %}
{{ tool('doc_search_text') }} lists the hits of a query in one text source, in page order, with the page of each hit.
{% endif %}
{% if has('pdf_search') %}
{{ tool('pdf_search') }} finds a query on the pages of a PDF source. Give page_from and page_to to search a range of pages.
{% endif %}

{% endif %}
{% if has('read_documents') %}
Read a page with {{ tool('read_documents') }} when the passage does not show enough text
to support the claim. Give its page, or give the query to open the page with the most hits.
{% endif %}

Give the document and page when a passage supports the answer.

{% if has('read_documents') %}
{{ tool('read_documents') }} requires collection and file_hash.
collection is one name. file_hash is a list of 1 to 20 hashes from that collection.
For documents in different collections, make a separate batch per collection.
Copy identities from results. A unique file name or path can also resolve a document.
source optionally selects an extracted source. Omission uses the preferred source.
page optionally selects a stored page identifier. Page identifiers can have gaps.
Omit page or give zero to select the page with most query hits, or the first stored page without a query.
query opens text around nearby distinct matched words on that page.
For exact wording, quote the phrase inside the query. A single matched value opens its first occurrence.
offset overrides the passage start. It counts Unicode characters from zero within that page.
length is a positive character count. Omission uses 6,000 characters.
source_version optionally verifies the returned source fingerprint. Copy it for a range reread.

The result returns text_range with start, exclusive end, total page characters and unit.
page_complete means that the range covers the whole page.
A cut marker means the tool delivered only part of the range. It does not mean the page ends there.
Use an item's more to continue that document. Use the top-level more to continue the remaining page or later pages.
Copy the returned handle exactly into {{ tool('read_more') }} as continuation.
Copy read_before or read_after as read_documents arguments for surrounding text. No offset calculation is required.
A repeated initial call returns the same text. Use continuation when more text is needed.
Stop reading when the passage provides enough evidence for the requested claim.

This minimal call opens the first stored page.
```json
{"collection":"alpha","file_hash":["COPY_RETURNED_HASH"]}
```
This call opens a targeted passage.
```json
{"collection":"alpha","file_hash":["COPY_RETURNED_HASH"],"query":"Greenvelope"}
```
This call opens a returned range in a selected source and page.
```json
{"collection":"alpha","file_hash":["COPY_RETURNED_HASH"],"source":"COPY_RETURNED_SOURCE","page":7,"offset":50000,"length":4000,"source_version":"COPY_RETURNED_SOURCE_VERSION"}
```
This continuation reads the next returned range. Use the actual issued handle.
```json
{"continuation":"COPY_RETURNED_MORE"}
```
{% endif %}
{% if has('doc_search_text') %}
{{ tool('doc_search_text') }} requires collection, file_hash and query. source optionally selects one extraction.
It returns page, ordinal, start, end and snippet for each hit. Offsets count characters within that page.
Copy a hit page and start into read_documents when the snippet needs more context.
Use read_more to retrieve remaining hits.
```json
{"collection":"alpha","file_hash":"COPY_RETURNED_HASH","query":"Greenvelope"}
```
```json
{"collection":"alpha","file_hash":"COPY_RETURNED_HASH","query":"Greenvelope","source":"COPY_RETURNED_SOURCE"}
```
{% endif %}
{% if has('doc_sources') %}
{{ tool('doc_sources') }} requires collection and file_hash. query optionally counts matching hits in each extraction.
It returns source names and stored page ranges. Copy a source name when selecting a particular extraction.
```json
{"collection":"alpha","file_hash":"COPY_RETURNED_HASH"}
```
```json
{"collection":"alpha","file_hash":"COPY_RETURNED_HASH","query":"Greenvelope"}
```
{% endif %}
{% if has('doc_diff_sources') %}
{{ tool('doc_diff_sources') }} requires collection, file_hash, source_a and source_b.
page_a and page_b optionally select pages. Omission selects the first stored page of each source.
The result is a unified text diff. Use read_more when it continues.
```json
{"collection":"alpha","file_hash":"COPY_RETURNED_HASH","source_a":"COPY_SOURCE_A","source_b":"COPY_SOURCE_B"}
```
```json
{"collection":"alpha","file_hash":"COPY_RETURNED_HASH","source_a":"COPY_SOURCE_A","source_b":"COPY_SOURCE_B","page_a":7,"page_b":7}
```
{% endif %}
{% if has('pdf_search') %}
{{ tool('pdf_search') }} requires collection, file_hash and query.
source optionally selects a PDF extraction. page_from and page_to optionally restrict the inclusive PDF page range.
Copy returned page positions. Use read_more for continued hits.
```json
{"collection":"alpha","file_hash":"COPY_RETURNED_HASH","query":"Greenvelope"}
```
```json
{"collection":"alpha","file_hash":"COPY_RETURNED_HASH","query":"Greenvelope","source":"COPY_RETURNED_SOURCE","page_from":7,"page_to":12}
```
{% endif %}
{% if has('search_passages') %}
{{ tool('search_passages') }} accepts queries as one string or a list of up to 12 forms.
collection accepts one name or a list. Omission searches every permitted collection.
max_results selects the hit count within the served schema limit. Omission uses 15.
The result gives collection, file_hash, page and snippet. q records the zero-based query indexes.
Read supporting text when the passage does not answer the question.
```json
{"queries":"approval of the transfer"}
```
```json
{"collection":["alpha","beta"],"queries":["approval of the transfer","transfer authorization"],"max_results":5}
```
{% endif %}
